31752448422141,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":-0.33573447399000067,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.06051013188700738,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":55.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.03925376309888162,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":5.4,"_gate_margins":0.0009345928525336382,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":50.9,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07755146515044334,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":97.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":50.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0007230049897580578,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.30185,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.969,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":96.9,"pf":[],"description_full":"Global Partners LP engages in the purchasing, selling, gathering, blending, storing, and logistics of transporting gasoline and gasoline blendstocks, distillates, residual oil, renewable fuels, crude oil, and propane to wholesalers, retailers, and commercial customers. The company operates through three segments: Wholesale, Gasoline Distribution and Station Operations (GDSO), and Commercial. The Wholesale segment sells home heating oil, branded and unbranded gasoline and gasoline blendstocks, diesel, kerosene, and residual oil to retailers and wholesale distributors. This segment transports the products by railcars, barges, trucks and/or pipelines. The GDSO segment sells branded and unbranded gasoline to gasoline station operators and sub-jobbers; operates convenience stores and prepared food sales; and provides car wash, lottery, and ATM services, as well as leases gasoline stations. The Commercial segment sells and delivers unbranded gasoline, home heating oil, diesel, kerosene, residual oil, and bunker fuel to customers in the public sector; and sells custom blended fuels. The company is involved in the transportation of petroleum products and renewable fuels through rail from the mid-continent region of the United States and Canada. Global Partners LP was founded in 2005 and is based in Waltham, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Eric S. Slifka | President, CEO & Chairman of Global GP LLC | Age 59 | Compensation: $5.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $5.7M ranks in the top quartile among Energy peers. Each employee generates $59K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Global Partners LP is a small-cap energy business with a $1.5B market cap on $18.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Gross margins of 6% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $193M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.91\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 30% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 14% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Energy peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 69% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Insiders are net buyers (97% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $7.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Global Partners (GLP) Moves to Strong Buy: Rationale Behind the Upgrade","source":"finance.yahoo.com","lin